import ../../../testing/driver.dl

document deferred input:
    view group "Mode" using no UI appearance:
        paragraph "Closed" using no UI appearance
        text field "Query" containing "Find" using no UI appearance

to show deferred input {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's input kind = 8:
        set the value of "Mode" in (view's instance) to 1
        set field to the UI layout labeled "Query" in (view's layout)
        activate UI layout field in view

set instance to an instance of deferred input
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 500 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
watch UI input in (the address of view) using (the function named "show deferred input $")
queue UI input of kind 8 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 4 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "x" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((the UI value for (the control labeled "Query" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text) = "Findx") reporting "A newly selected field lost queued text before painting"
require condition (view's input context's active) reporting "The selected field did not publish its input context"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Input observers can reveal and focus deferred fields before queued text and painting."
